// `src/hir/repr.npk` — THE HIR: A FLAT ARENA OF NINE KINDS OF NODE THAT OWN NOTHING.
// Cycle 0.2.0, RX-223 and RX-224; `meta/specs/HIR.md` rules H-2 … H-4.
//
// THE AST'S SHAPE, FOR THE AST'S REASON (`SYNTAX.md` Y-26, RX-174). The tree is a
// `Vec<HirNode>`, and a node names another by INDEX, never by pointer: a `Vec`
// reallocates as it grows and every pointer into it would dangle, while an index survives
// (H-3). A node owns nothing -- no `string`, no `Vec`, no pointer -- which is what lets a
// `Vec` hold it (`SAFETY.md` S-23a; `check_vec_elements_own_nothing` clears it by reading
// this file) and what lets `vec_get` hand it back by value (it derives `Copy`). A group's
// name is not a node's: it is copied once into `Hir.names`, and `GroupInfo` holds its
// offset and length there, so a HIR outlives the pattern it was built from.
//
// EVERY OPERAND IS `int64`, AND EVERY NODE HAS A `next` (RX-223). `HIR.md` H-2 drew three
// `int32` operands. Two things are wrong with that for this arena: the values come from
// `int64`s -- the AST's operands, a `Vec`'s count -- and the language has no checked
// narrowing (`=>!` truncates in silence), so an `int32` field needs a hand-written range
// check at every write; and three operands cannot hold a `Repeat`'s child, minimum and
// maximum AND the sibling a list needs. So the AST's answer is the HIR's too: `int64`
// operands and a `next`. FORTY BYTES, MEASURED -- `tests/unit/hir_size.npk` exits with
// `#size_of<HirNode>()` -- where H-2's drawing measures 20; a HIR is proportional to its
// pattern (H-7), so that is paid once per pattern, at compile time.
//
// NO POSITION. Unlike the AST, a node holds no offset into the pattern: structurally equal
// patterns must give literally equal HIRs (H-13), and an offset would tell `ab` from
// `(?:a)b`. A refusal made while the HIR is built takes its offset from the AST node it
// is building from (cycle 0.2.2's `RepeatProductTooLarge`).
//
// THE COMPUTED PROPERTIES ARE THIS FILE'S TO WRITE (cycle 0.2.4, RX-238, RX-239; `HIR.md` H-9, H-10,
// H-17 and H-18). Four facts of every node -- whether it may match the empty string, whether every
// match begins at the haystack's start or ends at its end, and whether it is a plain literal or a union
// of plain literals -- are cached in the high half of its `flags` by ONE bottom-up pass over the whole
// tree, and `hir_props` is the query: it runs the pass when the tree's facts are not computed yet, and
// then reads. `HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED` is the distinct "not yet computed" state, never `false`. `hir_push`
// and `hir_set` drop those bits from every node they are handed, so no builder writes a fact and a node
// copied from a computed tree carries none; and once the facts are computed the tree is finished --
// `hir_set` and `hir_set_root` stop on it, so a cached fact is never stale.
//
// AND THE LITERALS (cycle 0.2.5, RX-241, RX-242; `HIR.md` H-11, H-12, H-19 and H-20). The three a prefilter reads --
// the prefix every match begins with, the bytes a match may begin with, a literal every match holds -- each a fact of
// every match that errs towards saying less, are `Hir.literals`, `Literal`s whose bytes are in `Hir.lits`, written by
// the extraction below and by nothing else. `hir_literals` is the query: it extracts them when the `Hir` holds none --
// after the facts, so the tree is finished first -- and the first-byte set's entry is always written, so a `Hir` that
// holds none has not had them extracted: "not yet", never "no literal".
//
// THE ARENA IS THE COMPILER'S TO GUARD. Every field of `Hir` but `root` is `hidden` (the
// compiler's D-314): outside this file it cannot be read (NITPICK-TYPE-080,
// `tests/rejection/hir_nodes_read.npk`), so every access goes through the functions below
// -- `vec_get`, `vec_set`, `vec_push`, `bytes_get` underneath, the only bounds check this
// library has (S-23). `root` is `sealed`: read anywhere, set only by `hir_set_root`.
//
// LAYERING (`BUILD.md` §6, B-16). Imports `core`, whose eleven arms a program importing
// this file owes, and `unicode` for `ClassRange` (RX-222), which adds none.
mod:repr;

use "../core/core.npk".*;
use "../unicode/unicode.npk".*;

// The index that names no node: an absent sibling, an unbounded repetition's maximum, and
// the root of a `Hir` that nothing has been built into.
pub fixed int64:HIR_NONE = -1i64;

// The flag bits (RX-223). Each belongs to its kinds, as the AST's per-kind bits do (Y-26);
// cycle 0.2.4's computed properties (H-9) take bits above them. NO PATTERN FLAG SURVIVES
// HERE (H-6): `m` is an `Anchor`'s value, `s` a `.`'s class, `i` folded ranges, `x` the
// parser's -- and `u` is `HIR_FLAG_BYTE`, which says what a node MATCHES, a byte rather than
// a codepoint, never how to read anything at run time.
pub fixed uint32:HIR_FLAG_LAZY = 1u32;   // a `Repeat` that prefers fewer iterations
pub fixed uint32:HIR_FLAG_BYTE = 2u32;   // a `Literal` that is a byte, a `Class` of bytes, a `WordBoundary` over ASCII
// *(2026-10-13, cycle 0.2.4 -- RX-239: *"bits above them"* are the high half, `HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED` and the
// four facts below, where no AST flag is -- `ast.npk`'s are 1 … 1024 -- so no AST flag copied into a node
// lands on one, and the dump refuses each it refused (RX-227).)*

// THE COMPUTED PROPERTIES (H-9, H-17, H-18; RX-238, RX-239). A node whose `HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED` is clear
// holds no fact -- the distinct "not yet computed" state -- and one whose bit is set holds its four.
// Every kind takes all five; only this file's pass writes them, and the dump writes none (H-15).
pub fixed uint32:HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED = 65536u32;            // the four bits above it are the node's facts
pub fixed uint32:HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY = 131072u32;          // the subtree may match the empty string
pub fixed uint32:HIR_IS_ANCHORED_START = 262144u32;        // every match begins at the haystack's start
pub fixed uint32:HIR_IS_ANCHORED_END = 524288u32;          // every match ends at the haystack's end
pub fixed uint32:HIR_IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL = 1048576u32;  // a plain literal, or a union of plain literals
pub fixed uint32:HIR_PROPS = 1966080u32;                   // the four facts: what `hir_props` answers
pub fixed uint32:HIR_COMPUTED = 2031616u32;                // the four and `HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED`: the pass's alone

// An `Anchor`'s `a` (`SYNTAX.md` §6, `m` erased).
pub fixed int64:HIR_TEXT_START = 0i64;   // the haystack's start: `^`, `\A`
pub fixed int64:HIR_TEXT_END = 1i64;     // the haystack's end: `$`, `\z`
pub fixed int64:HIR_LINE_START = 2i64;   // the haystack's start and after every `\n`: `^` under `m`
pub fixed int64:HIR_LINE_END = 3i64;     // the haystack's end and before every `\n`: `$` under `m`

// A `WordBoundary`'s `a` (`UNICODE.md` §5); under `HIR_FLAG_BYTE` a word character is ASCII's.
pub fixed int64:HIR_WORD = 0i64;         // `\b`
pub fixed int64:HIR_NOT_WORD = 1i64;     // `\B`

// `HIR.md` H-4's closed list, in its order; what each kind's operands hold is H-4a's table
// (RX-223). `tests/unit/hir_unit.npk` holds this list to the order with an exhaustive `pick`.
#[derive(Copy)]
pub enum:HirKind = {
    Empty;
    Literal;
    Class;
    Concat;
    Alternate;
    Repeat;
    Group;
    Anchor;
    WordBoundary;
};

#[derive(Copy)]
pub struct:HirNode = {
    HirKind:kind;      // H-4
    uint32:flags;      // the HIR_FLAG_ bits
    int64:a;           // H-2's operands, by kind
    int64:b;
    int64:c;
    int64:next;        // the next sibling in its parent's list, or HIR_NONE
};

// One capture group's entry in `Hir.groups` (RX-224): its name, as an offset and a length in
// `Hir.names`. `groups[k]` is group `k`; group 0 is the whole match, which has no name.
#[derive(Copy)]
pub struct:GroupInfo = {
    int64:off;         // the name's first byte in `Hir.names`
    int64:len;         // its length; 0 when the group has no name
};

// A literal's role (H-11, H-19): what it says of every match of the tree it was extracted from.
pub fixed int64:HIR_LITERAL_PREFIX = 0i64;     // every match begins with its bytes
pub fixed int64:HIR_LITERAL_WHOLE = 1i64;      // every match is its bytes: the prefix, when it is a whole match
pub fixed int64:HIR_LITERAL_FIRST = 2i64;      // every match begins with one of its bytes, which ascend
pub fixed int64:HIR_LITERAL_ANYWHERE = 3i64;   // no first-byte set: a match may begin anywhere, the end included
pub fixed int64:HIR_LITERAL_INNER = 4i64;      // every match holds its bytes

// One of a `Hir`'s literals (H-20): its role, and its bytes -- `len` of them from `off` in `Hir.lits` -- so it
// owns nothing, as a group's name is an offset and a length in `Hir.names` (`SAFETY.md` S-23a, RX-224).
#[derive(Copy)]
pub struct:Literal = {
    int64:role;        // HIR_LITERAL_PREFIX … HIR_LITERAL_INNER
    int64:off;         // its first byte in `Hir.lits`
    int64:len;         // how many bytes
};

// MOVE-ONLY, because it holds a `Vec` and a `Bytes` (`SAFETY.md` S-23b, RX-161): transfer
// it with `move(...)`, lend it by value to a reader, hand it by pointer to anything that
// changes it.
pub struct:Hir = {
    hidden Vec<HirNode>:nodes;       // the arena
    hidden Vec<ClassRange>:ranges;   // every class's ranges, contiguous per class
    hidden Bytes:names;              // the groups' names, one after another
    hidden Vec<GroupInfo>:groups;    // one entry per group, group 0 first
    hidden Vec<Literal>:literals;    // H-11's literals, in its order, once extracted; none until then (H-20)
    hidden Vec<uint8>:lits;          // the literals' bytes, one after another
    sealed int64:root;               // the root node, HIR_NONE until a builder sets it
};

// obligation: never fails ensures result.root == HIR_NONE && hir_len(result) == 0i64 && hir_group_count(result) == 1i64
//
// An empty arena, and group 0's entry: the whole match is a group, numbered 0, with no name
// (`COMPILE.md` C-16), so a group the pattern opens is numbered from 1, as Y-6 numbers it.
pub func:hir_init = Hir(int64:cap) never fails {
    Hir:h = Hir{ nodes: raw vec_init::<HirNode>(cap), ranges: raw vec_init::<ClassRange>(cap),
                 names: raw bytes_init(cap), groups: raw vec_init::<GroupInfo>(cap),
                 literals: raw vec_init::<Literal>(cap), lits: raw vec_init::<uint8>(cap), root: HIR_NONE };
    drop vec_push(@h.groups, GroupInfo{ off: 0i64, len: 0i64 });
    pass h;
};

// obligation: never fails ensures result == h.nodes.count
pub func:hir_len = int64(Hir:h) never fails {
    pass h.nodes.count;
};

// obligation: never fails ensures hir_len(h) == old(hir_len(h)) + 1i64 && result == hir_len(h) - 1i64
//
// Appends a node and answers its index -- its computed bits dropped: a fact is the pass's to write
// (H-18), and a node copied from a computed tree would carry that tree's.
pub func:hir_push = int64(Hir->:h, HirNode:n) never fails {
    HirNode:x = n;
    x.flags = n.flags & (~HIR_COMPUTED);
    drop vec_push(@h.nodes, x);
    pass h.nodes.count - 1i64;
};

// obligation: never fails requires i >= 0i64 && i < hir_len(h)
pub func:hir_get = HirNode(Hir:h, int64:i) never fails {
    pass raw vec_get(h.nodes, i);
};

// Whether `h`'s facts are computed: its root's -- the pass leaves the root last, after every node under it.
func:facts_done = bool(Hir->:h) never fails {
    if (h.root == HIR_NONE) { pass false; }
    HirNode:r = raw vec_get(h.nodes, h.root);
    pass (r.flags & HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED) != 0u32;
};

// obligation: never fails requires i >= 0i64 && i < hir_len(h)
//
// Rewrites a node, its computed bits dropped (H-18). A tree whose facts are computed is finished, and a
// write to it stops `OutOfBounds`: a fact cached in it is never stale (H-10).
pub func:hir_set = NIL(Hir->:h, int64:i, HirNode:n) never fails {
    if (raw facts_done(h)) { drop vec_oob(i); }
    HirNode:x = n;
    x.flags = n.flags & (~HIR_COMPUTED);
    drop vec_set(@h.nodes, i, x);
    pass NIL;
};

// obligation: never fails requires i >= 0i64 && i < hir_len(h)
//
// Sets the root -- and stops `OutOfBounds` on a tree whose facts are computed (H-18), as `hir_set` does.
pub func:hir_set_root = NIL(Hir->:h, int64:i) never fails {
    if (i < 0i64)           { drop vec_oob(i); }
    if (i >= h.nodes.count) { drop vec_oob(i); }
    if (raw facts_done(h))  { drop vec_oob(i); }
    h.root = i;
    pass NIL;
};

// obligation: never fails ensures result == h.ranges.count
pub func:hir_range_count = int64(Hir:h) never fails {
    pass h.ranges.count;
};

// obligation: never fails ensures hir_range_count(h) == old(hir_range_count(h)) + 1i64 && result == hir_range_count(h) - 1i64
//
// Appends a class range and answers its index. A `Class` node names its ranges by the first
// one's index and how many, so a builder pushes a class's ranges one after another.
pub func:hir_push_range = int64(Hir->:h, ClassRange:r) never fails {
    drop vec_push(@h.ranges, r);
    pass h.ranges.count - 1i64;
};

// obligation: never fails requires i >= 0i64 && i < hir_range_count(h)
pub func:hir_range = ClassRange(Hir:h, int64:i) never fails {
    pass raw vec_get(h.ranges, i);
};

// obligation: never fails ensures result == h.groups.count
//
// How many groups, group 0 among them: one more than the pattern's capturing groups.
pub func:hir_group_count = int64(Hir:h) never fails {
    pass h.groups.count;
};

// obligation: never fails ensures hir_group_count(h) == old(hir_group_count(h)) + 1i64 && result == hir_group_count(h) - 1i64
//
// The next group, its name copied into `Hir.names` -- an empty `name` for a group that has
// none -- answering its number.
pub func:hir_add_group = int64(Hir->:h, fixed uint8[]:name) never fails {
    int64:off = raw bytes_len(@h.names);
    drop bytes_extend(@h.names, name);
    drop vec_push(@h.groups, GroupInfo{ off: off, len: name.len });
    pass h.groups.count - 1i64;
};

// obligation: never fails requires k >= 0i64 && k < hir_group_count(h)
pub func:hir_group = GroupInfo(Hir:h, int64:k) never fails {
    pass raw vec_get(h.groups, k);
};

// obligation: never fails requires hir_group_count(to) == 1i64
//
// Copies `from`'s groups past group 0 into `to`, in number order, each one's name into `to`'s
// names: the table a pass that keeps every group keeps (cycle 0.2.3's normalisation, H-13). Pass a
// `to` fresh from `hir_init`.
pub func:hir_copy_groups = NIL(Hir->:from, Hir->:to) never fails {
    int64:k = 1i64;
    while (k < from.groups.count) decreases from.groups.count - k {
        GroupInfo:g = raw vec_get(from.groups, k);
        int64:off = raw bytes_len(@to.names);
        int64:i = 0i64;
        while (i < g.len) decreases g.len - i {
            drop bytes_push(@to.names, raw bytes_get(@from.names, g.off + i));
            i = i + 1i64;
        }
        drop vec_push(@to.groups, GroupInfo{ off: off, len: g.len });
        k = k + 1i64;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// obligation: never fails requires k >= 0i64 && k < hir_group_count(h)
//
// Appends group `k`'s name to `out`: nothing for a group with none. The bytes are copied --
// a view of `Hir.names` could not be handed back (D-004).
pub func:hir_put_name = NIL(Hir->:h, int64:k, Bytes->:out) never fails {
    GroupInfo:g = raw vec_get(h.groups, k);
    int64:i = 0i64;
    while (i < g.len) decreases g.len - i {
        drop bytes_push(out, raw bytes_get(@h.names, g.off + i));
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// ---- the computed properties (H-9, H-10, H-17, H-18; RX-238, RX-239) ----------------------------------

// One step of the facts' walk: a node to enter, or one whose children are done, to leave.
#[derive(Copy)]
struct:FactStep = {
    int64:node;          // the node
    int64:op;            // FACT_ONE, FACT_LIST or FACT_LEAVE
};

fixed int64:FACT_ONE = 0i64;       // enter the node
fixed int64:FACT_LIST = 1i64;      // enter the node, then the rest of the list it heads
fixed int64:FACT_LEAVE = 2i64;     // its children are done: its facts

// H-17, A `Concat` OR AN `Alternate`: from its members' facts, in the order its chain links them. A
// `Concat` may match the empty string when every piece may, begins at the start when its first piece
// does and ends at the end when its last does, and is a plain literal -- a literal run -- when it holds
// a piece and every piece is a `Literal`. An `Alternate` may match the empty string when an alternative
// may, and, holding one alternative or more, is anchored at either end when every alternative is, and a
// union of plain literals when every alternative is a plain literal: a `Literal` or a literal run.
func:list_facts = uint32(Hir->:h, HirNode:n) never fails {
    bool:every_empty = true;
    bool:some_empty = false;
    bool:every_start = true;
    bool:every_end = true;
    bool:first_start = false;
    bool:last_end = false;
    bool:every_literal = true;
    bool:every_plain = true;
    int64:m = n.a;
    int64:k = 0i64;
    while ((m != HIR_NONE) && (k < n.b)) decreases n.b - k {
        HirNode:x = raw vec_get(h.nodes, m);
        bool:e = (x.flags & HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY) != 0u32;
        bool:s = (x.flags & HIR_IS_ANCHORED_START) != 0u32;
        bool:t = (x.flags & HIR_IS_ANCHORED_END) != 0u32;
        bool:lit = x.kind == HirKind.Literal;
        bool:run = (x.kind == HirKind.Concat) && ((x.flags & HIR_IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL) != 0u32);
        every_empty = every_empty && e;
        some_empty = some_empty || e;
        every_start = every_start && s;
        every_end = every_end && t;
        if (k == 0i64) { first_start = s; }
        last_end = t;
        every_literal = every_literal && lit;
        every_plain = every_plain && (lit || run);
        m = x.next;
        k = k + 1i64;
    }
    uint32:f = 0u32;
    if (n.kind == HirKind.Concat) {
        if (every_empty) { f = f | HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY; }
        if (first_start) { f = f | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_START; }
        if (last_end) { f = f | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_END; }
        if ((k > 0i64) && every_literal) { f = f | HIR_IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL; }
        pass f;
    }
    if (some_empty) { f = f | HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY; }
    if (k > 0i64) {
        if (every_start) { f = f | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_START; }
        if (every_end) { f = f | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_END; }
        if (every_plain) { f = f | HIR_IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL; }
    }
    pass f;
};

// H-17, ONE NODE: its four facts from its kind, its operands and its children's facts, which the walk
// below has computed before it. No fact reads `HIR_FLAG_BYTE` or `HIR_FLAG_LAZY`, or a class's ranges.
func:facts_of = uint32(Hir->:h, HirNode:n) never fails {
    if (n.kind == HirKind.Empty)        { pass HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY; }
    if (n.kind == HirKind.Literal)      { pass HIR_IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL; }
    if (n.kind == HirKind.Class)        { pass 0u32; }
    if (n.kind == HirKind.WordBoundary) { pass HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY; }
    if (n.kind == HirKind.Anchor) {
        // `^` and `\A` are `HIR_TEXT_START`, `$` and `\z` `HIR_TEXT_END`; under `m`, `^` and `$` are the
        // lines' anchors, which hold after and before every `\n` too (`SYNTAX.md` §6), and anchor nothing
        uint32:f = HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY;
        if (n.a == HIR_TEXT_START) { f = f | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_START; }
        if (n.a == HIR_TEXT_END)   { f = f | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_END; }
        pass f;
    }
    if ((n.kind == HirKind.Repeat) || (n.kind == HirKind.Group)) {
        // a `Group` is its body's, but no plain literal; a `Repeat` of minimum 0 may match the empty
        // string and anchors nothing, and one of minimum 1 or more is its body's, and no plain literal
        if ((n.kind == HirKind.Repeat) && (n.b == 0i64)) { pass HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY; }
        HirNode:c = raw vec_get(h.nodes, n.a);
        pass c.flags & (HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_START | HIR_IS_ANCHORED_END);
    }
    pass raw list_facts(h, n);
};

// THE ONE PASS (H-10): every node of the tree under the root, each after its children, on an explicit
// stack (`SAFETY.md` S-19) bounded by twice the arena, as the build's, the dump's and the normaliser's
// walks are, so a node that holds itself stops it `DecreasesViolated`. Each node it leaves gets
// `HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED` and its facts, the root last; a node it leaves computed already stops it
// `OutOfBounds` -- a node with two parents, or a second pass over one tree, which `hir_props` never makes.
func:compute_facts = NIL(Hir->:h) never fails {
    Vec<FactStep>:todo = raw vec_init::<FactStep>(16i64);
    drop vec_push(@todo, FactStep{ node: h.root, op: FACT_ONE });
    // A `decreases` measure is checked as each step begins, so `2n - 1` admits `2n` steps: a walk
    // entering and leaving every node of the arena once, and not one more.
    int64:budget = 2i64 * h.nodes.count - 1i64;
    int64:steps = 0i64;
    while (todo.count > 0i64) decreases budget - steps {
        steps = steps + 1i64;
        FactStep:s = raw vec_pop(@todo);
        HirNode:n = raw vec_get(h.nodes, s.node);
        if (s.op == FACT_LEAVE) {
            if ((n.flags & HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED) != 0u32) { drop vec_oob(s.node); }
            n.flags = n.flags | HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED | (raw facts_of(h, n));
            drop vec_set(@h.nodes, s.node, n);
        }
        else {
            if ((s.op == FACT_LIST) && (n.next != HIR_NONE)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, FactStep{ node: n.next, op: FACT_LIST });
            }
            drop vec_push(@todo, FactStep{ node: s.node, op: FACT_LEAVE });
            if ((n.kind == HirKind.Concat) || (n.kind == HirKind.Alternate)) {
                if (n.a != HIR_NONE) { drop vec_push(@todo, FactStep{ node: n.a, op: FACT_LIST }); }
            }
            else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Repeat) || (n.kind == HirKind.Group)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, FactStep{ node: n.a, op: FACT_ONE });
            }
        }
    }
    drop vec_free(@todo);
    pass NIL;
};

// obligation: never fails requires h.root != HIR_NONE && i >= 0i64 && i < hir_len(h) && i is reached from h.root
//
// THE QUERY (H-10, H-18): node `i`'s four facts, `HIR_PROPS`' bits -- computed first, by the one pass
// over the whole tree, when the tree's are not; read once they are. NO CALLER COMPUTES FIRST (the
// compiler's D-227: the query ensures, and the caller does not remember). A `Hir` with no root, and a node
// the root does not reach, have no facts: each stops `OutOfBounds`, and neither is ever answered with no
// bits, which would read "not computed" as "false".
pub func:hir_props = uint32(Hir->:h, int64:i) never fails {
    if (h.root == HIR_NONE) { drop vec_oob(i); }
    if (!(raw facts_done(h))) { drop compute_facts(h); }
    HirNode:n = raw vec_get(h.nodes, i);
    if ((n.flags & HIR_PROPS_COMPUTED) == 0u32) { drop vec_oob(i); }
    pass n.flags & HIR_PROPS;
};

// ---- the literals (H-11, H-12, H-19, H-20) ------------------------------------------------------------

// How many bytes a match of a `Literal` holding `cp` has (H-19): its UTF-8 encoding's, or under `byte` one --
// `UNICODE.md` U-18 and U-19, a Unicode-mode node matches its well-formed encoding alone.
func:cp_len = int64(int64:cp, bool:byte) never fails {
    if (byte) { pass 1i64; }
    if ((cp >> 7i64) == 0i64) { pass 1i64; }
    if ((cp >> 11i64) == 0i64) { pass 2i64; }
    if ((cp >> 16i64) == 0i64) { pass 3i64; }
    pass 4i64;
};

// And its byte `i`, `0 <= i < cp_len`: the encoding's lead byte, then each continuation byte, six bits of the
// codepoint each, or under `byte` the byte. A surrogate, which only a text `hir_read` reads can hold
// (`COMPILE.md` C-3), is the three bytes this arithmetic gives, which no well-formed haystack holds.
func:cp_byte = uint8(int64:cp, bool:byte, int64:i) never fails {
    int64:k = raw cp_len(cp, byte);
    if (k == 1i64) { pass cp =>! uint8; }
    if (i == 0i64) {
        if (k == 2i64) { pass (192i64 | (cp >> 6i64)) =>! uint8; }
        if (k == 3i64) { pass (224i64 | (cp >> 12i64)) =>! uint8; }
        pass (240i64 | (cp >> 18i64)) =>! uint8;
    }
    pass (128i64 | ((cp >> (6i64 * (k - 1i64 - i))) & 63i64)) =>! uint8;
};

// Adds to `s` the bytes `from` … `to`.
func:add_span = NIL(ByteSet->:s, int64:from, int64:to) never fails {
    int64:b = from;
    while (b <= to) decreases to - b {
        drop byteset_add(s, b =>! uint8);
        b = b + 1i64;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Adds to `s` the first byte of every member of a class's range `lo` … `hi` (H-19): under `byte` each byte
// itself; else each codepoint's lead byte. An ASCII codepoint is its own byte, and past U+007F a lead byte rises
// with the codepoint over one run of bytes, `C2` … `F4` -- each the lead of an interval of codepoints, the
// intervals adjacent (`COMPILE.md` C-2) -- so a range past it has its ends' lead bytes and every byte between.
// Only the ASCII edge splits a range: `7F` and `C2` are not adjacent.
func:add_leads = NIL(ByteSet->:s, int64:lo, int64:hi, bool:byte) never fails {
    if (byte) { drop add_span(s, lo, hi); pass NIL; }
    if (lo <= 127i64) {
        int64:top = hi;
        if (top > 127i64) { top = 127i64; }
        drop add_span(s, lo, top);
    }
    if (hi >= 128i64) {
        int64:from = lo;
        if (from < 128i64) { from = 128i64; }
        drop add_span(s, (raw cp_byte(from, false, 0i64)) => int64, (raw cp_byte(hi, false, 0i64)) => int64);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// One step of a literal walk: a node, and what the walk does with it.
#[derive(Copy)]
struct:LitStep = {
    int64:node;          // the node
    int64:op;            // LIT_ONE, LIT_PIECE, LIT_ALT or LIT_AFTER
};

fixed int64:LIT_ONE = 0i64;      // the node
fixed int64:LIT_PIECE = 1i64;    // a `Concat`'s piece: the node, then the piece after it
fixed int64:LIT_ALT = 2i64;      // an `Alternate`'s alternative: the node, then the one after it
fixed int64:LIT_AFTER = 3i64;    // a `Repeat`'s body read once: whether the prefix goes on

// THE FIRST-BYTE SET (H-19): into `s`, the first byte of every match of the tree under the root -- a `Literal`'s
// first byte, a `Class`'s members' first bytes, a `Group`'s and a `Repeat`'s body's, an `Alternate`'s every
// alternative's, and a `Concat`'s pieces' up to the first that cannot match the empty string, that one's too;
// an `Empty`, an `Anchor` and a `WordBoundary` none. Whether a piece may match the empty string is H-17's fact,
// read through `hir_props`: it says MAY, so it errs this set's way -- a byte more, never one fewer. A tree
// visits each node once, so the walk is bounded by the arena.
func:first_bytes = NIL(Hir->:h, ByteSet->:s) never fails {
    Vec<LitStep>:todo = raw vec_init::<LitStep>(16i64);
    drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: h.root, op: LIT_ONE });
    int64:budget = h.nodes.count - 1i64;
    int64:steps = 0i64;
    while (todo.count > 0i64) decreases budget - steps {
        steps = steps + 1i64;
        LitStep:t = raw vec_pop(@todo);
        HirNode:n = raw vec_get(h.nodes, t.node);
        bool:byte = (n.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32;
        if ((t.op == LIT_PIECE) && (n.next != HIR_NONE)) {
            if (((raw hir_props(h, t.node)) & HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY) != 0u32) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.next, op: LIT_PIECE });
            }
        }
        else if ((t.op == LIT_ALT) && (n.next != HIR_NONE)) {
            drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.next, op: LIT_ALT });
        }
        if (n.kind == HirKind.Literal) {
            drop byteset_add(s, raw cp_byte(n.a, byte, 0i64));
        }
        else if (n.kind == HirKind.Class) {
            int64:r = 0i64;
            while (r < n.b) decreases n.b - r {
                ClassRange:x = raw vec_get(h.ranges, n.a + r);
                drop add_leads(s, x.lo => int64, x.hi => int64, byte);
                r = r + 1i64;
            }
        }
        else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Group) || (n.kind == HirKind.Repeat)) {
            drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_ONE });
        }
        else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Concat) && (n.a != HIR_NONE)) {
            drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_PIECE });
        }
        else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Alternate) && (n.a != HIR_NONE)) {
            drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_ALT });
        }
    }
    drop vec_free(@todo);
    pass NIL;
};

// A plain literal's bytes (H-17's plain literal: a `Literal`, or a `Concat` of `Literal`s) appended to
// `Hir.lits`, `room` of them at most; answers how many it has, written or not.
func:plain_put = int64(Hir->:h, int64:i, int64:room) never fails {
    HirNode:x = raw vec_get(h.nodes, i);
    int64:p = i;
    int64:count = 1i64;
    if (x.kind == HirKind.Concat) { p = x.a; count = x.b; }
    int64:total = 0i64;
    int64:j = 0i64;
    while ((p != HIR_NONE) && (j < count)) decreases count - j {
        HirNode:y = raw vec_get(h.nodes, p);
        bool:byte = (y.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32;
        int64:k = raw cp_len(y.a, byte);
        int64:q = 0i64;
        while (q < k) decreases k - q {
            if (total < room) { drop vec_push(@h.lits, raw cp_byte(y.a, byte, q)); }
            total = total + 1i64;
            q = q + 1i64;
        }
        p = y.next;
        j = j + 1i64;
    }
    pass total;
};

// How many of a plain literal's first bytes are `Hir.lits`' from `at` on, `bound` at most.
func:plain_common = int64(Hir->:h, int64:i, int64:at, int64:bound) never fails {
    HirNode:x = raw vec_get(h.nodes, i);
    int64:p = i;
    int64:count = 1i64;
    if (x.kind == HirKind.Concat) { p = x.a; count = x.b; }
    int64:same = 0i64;
    int64:j = 0i64;
    while ((p != HIR_NONE) && (j < count)) decreases count - j {
        HirNode:y = raw vec_get(h.nodes, p);
        bool:byte = (y.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32;
        int64:k = raw cp_len(y.a, byte);
        int64:q = 0i64;
        while (q < k) decreases k - q {
            if (same >= bound) { pass same; }
            if ((raw vec_get(h.lits, at + same)) != (raw cp_byte(y.a, byte, q))) { pass same; }
            same = same + 1i64;
            q = q + 1i64;
        }
        p = y.next;
        j = j + 1i64;
    }
    pass same;
};

// How many bytes a plain literal has.
func:plain_len = int64(Hir->:h, int64:i) never fails {
    HirNode:x = raw vec_get(h.nodes, i);
    int64:p = i;
    int64:count = 1i64;
    if (x.kind == HirKind.Concat) { p = x.a; count = x.b; }
    int64:total = 0i64;
    int64:j = 0i64;
    while ((p != HIR_NONE) && (j < count)) decreases count - j {
        HirNode:y = raw vec_get(h.nodes, p);
        total = total + (raw cp_len(y.a, (y.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32));
        p = y.next;
        j = j + 1i64;
    }
    pass total;
};

// AN `Alternate` IN THE PREFIX (H-19). When every alternative is a plain literal -- a `Literal` or a `Concat`
// holding H-17's `IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL`, whose words are the plain literal's; the fact says the shape, the
// tree which bytes -- appends the bytes they all begin with, at most what `NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES` leaves the
// prefix from `base`, and answers whether the read goes on: every alternative the same bytes, all written. Any
// other alternative, and an `Alternate` of none, appends nothing and stops the read.
func:shared_start = bool(Hir->:h, HirNode:n, int64:base) never fails {
    if ((n.b == 0i64) || (n.a == HIR_NONE)) { pass false; }
    int64:m = n.a;
    int64:k = 0i64;
    while ((m != HIR_NONE) && (k < n.b)) decreases n.b - k {
        HirNode:x = raw vec_get(h.nodes, m);
        bool:shape = (x.kind == HirKind.Literal) || (x.kind == HirKind.Concat);
        if ((!shape) || (((raw hir_props(h, m)) & HIR_IS_ALTERNATION_LITERAL) == 0u32)) { pass false; }
        m = x.next;
        k = k + 1i64;
    }
    int64:start = h.lits.count;
    int64:total = raw plain_put(h, n.a, NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES - (start - base));
    int64:common = h.lits.count - start;
    bool:same = total == common;
    HirNode:first = raw vec_get(h.nodes, n.a);
    m = first.next;
    k = 1i64;
    while ((m != HIR_NONE) && (k < n.b)) decreases n.b - k {
        common = raw plain_common(h, m, start, common);
        if ((common != total) || ((raw plain_len(h, m)) != total)) { same = false; }
        HirNode:y = raw vec_get(h.nodes, m);
        m = y.next;
        k = k + 1i64;
    }
    drop vec_truncate(@h.lits, start + common);
    pass same;
};

// THE PREFIX (H-19): into `Hir.lits`, from its end, the bytes every match of the tree under the root begins
// with, read down from the root while every match of what is read is the same bytes -- a `Literal` its bytes;
// an `Empty`, an `Anchor` and a `WordBoundary` none, zero-width; a `Group` its body's; a `Concat` its pieces' in
// order; a `Repeat` of minimum 1 or more its body's once, going on only when its maximum is 1 -- `{1}`, its
// minimum at most its maximum; an `Alternate`, `shared_start` -- and stopping at a `Class`, a `Repeat` of minimum
// 0, and the byte past `NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES`. Answers whether the read reached the tree's end: every match is then
// those bytes, a whole match (RX-224). Each node is read once and a `Repeat` once more, so the walk is bounded by
// twice the arena.
func:prefix_bytes = bool(Hir->:h) never fails {
    int64:base = h.lits.count;
    Vec<LitStep>:todo = raw vec_init::<LitStep>(16i64);
    drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: h.root, op: LIT_ONE });
    int64:budget = 2i64 * h.nodes.count - 1i64;
    int64:steps = 0i64;
    bool:going = true;
    while (going && (todo.count > 0i64)) decreases budget - steps {
        steps = steps + 1i64;
        LitStep:t = raw vec_pop(@todo);
        HirNode:n = raw vec_get(h.nodes, t.node);
        if (t.op == LIT_AFTER) {
            if (n.c != 1i64) { going = false; }
        }
        else {
            if ((t.op == LIT_PIECE) && (n.next != HIR_NONE)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.next, op: LIT_PIECE });
            }
            if (n.kind == HirKind.Literal) {
                bool:byte = (n.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32;
                int64:k = raw cp_len(n.a, byte);
                int64:i = 0i64;
                while (going && (i < k)) decreases k - i {
                    if ((h.lits.count - base) >= NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES) { going = false; }
                    else {
                        drop vec_push(@h.lits, raw cp_byte(n.a, byte, i));
                        i = i + 1i64;
                    }
                }
            }
            else if (n.kind == HirKind.Class) { going = false; }
            else if (n.kind == HirKind.Group) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_ONE });
            }
            else if (n.kind == HirKind.Repeat) {
                if (n.b == 0i64) { going = false; }
                else {
                    drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: t.node, op: LIT_AFTER });
                    drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_ONE });
                }
            }
            else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Concat) && (n.a != HIR_NONE)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_PIECE });
            }
            else if (n.kind == HirKind.Alternate) { going = raw shared_start(h, n, base); }
        }
    }
    drop vec_free(@todo);
    pass going;
};

// THE INNER LITERAL (H-19): of the prefix -- `plen` bytes from `pfrom` in `Hir.lits` -- and every literal run the
// tree requires, the longest, counting `NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES` at most; of two as long, the prefix, then the run
// read first. A required node: the root, a `Group`'s body, a `Repeat`'s of minimum 1 or more and a `Concat`'s
// every piece -- never an `Alternate`'s alternative, nor a `Repeat`'s of minimum 0. A run: the adjacent
// `Literal` pieces of one `Concat` (RX-235), or a required `Literal` alone. Writes its entry when it has a byte,
// the prefix's bytes its own. A tree visits each node once, so the walk is bounded by the arena.
func:inner_literal = NIL(Hir->:h, int64:pfrom, int64:plen) never fails {
    int64:best = plen;
    int64:run_at = HIR_NONE;
    int64:run_count = 0i64;
    Vec<LitStep>:todo = raw vec_init::<LitStep>(16i64);
    drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: h.root, op: LIT_ONE });
    int64:budget = h.nodes.count - 1i64;
    int64:steps = 0i64;
    while (todo.count > 0i64) decreases budget - steps {
        steps = steps + 1i64;
        LitStep:t = raw vec_pop(@todo);
        HirNode:n = raw vec_get(h.nodes, t.node);
        if (n.kind == HirKind.Literal) {
            int64:count = 1i64;
            int64:len = raw cp_len(n.a, (n.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32);
            int64:m = HIR_NONE;
            if (t.op == LIT_PIECE) { m = n.next; }
            bool:more = true;
            while (more && (m != HIR_NONE)) decreases budget - steps {
                HirNode:y = raw vec_get(h.nodes, m);
                if (y.kind == HirKind.Literal) {
                    steps = steps + 1i64;
                    count = count + 1i64;
                    len = len + (raw cp_len(y.a, (y.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32));
                    m = y.next;
                }
                else { more = false; }
            }
            if (len > NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES) { len = NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES; }
            if (len > best) {
                best = len;
                run_at = t.node;
                run_count = count;
            }
            if (m != HIR_NONE) { drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: m, op: LIT_PIECE }); }
        }
        else {
            if ((t.op == LIT_PIECE) && (n.next != HIR_NONE)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.next, op: LIT_PIECE });
            }
            if (n.kind == HirKind.Group) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_ONE });
            }
            else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Repeat) && (n.b > 0i64)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_ONE });
            }
            else if ((n.kind == HirKind.Concat) && (n.a != HIR_NONE)) {
                drop vec_push(@todo, LitStep{ node: n.a, op: LIT_PIECE });
            }
        }
    }
    drop vec_free(@todo);
    if (best == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (run_at == HIR_NONE) {
        drop vec_push(@h.literals, Literal{ role: HIR_LITERAL_INNER, off: pfrom, len: plen });
        pass NIL;
    }
    int64:off = h.lits.count;
    int64:p = run_at;
    int64:j = 0i64;
    while ((p != HIR_NONE) && (j < run_count)) decreases run_count - j {
        HirNode:y = raw vec_get(h.nodes, p);
        bool:byte = (y.flags & HIR_FLAG_BYTE) != 0u32;
        int64:k = raw cp_len(y.a, byte);
        int64:q = 0i64;
        while (q < k) decreases k - q {
            if ((h.lits.count - off) < NREGEX_LITERAL_BYTES) { drop vec_push(@h.lits, raw cp_byte(y.a, byte, q)); }
            q = q + 1i64;
        }
        p = y.next;
        j = j + 1i64;
    }
    drop vec_push(@h.literals, Literal{ role: HIR_LITERAL_INNER, off: off, len: h.lits.count - off });
    pass NIL;
};

// THE EXTRACTION (H-19, H-20). The tree's facts first, through `hir_props` -- the one pass, which stops on an
// arena that is not a tree, and leaves the tree finished (H-18), so no literal written below is ever stale --
// then H-11's three into `Hir.lits` and `Hir.literals`, in its order: the prefix when it has a byte, `WHOLE` when
// the read reached the tree's end; the first-byte set always -- `ANYWHERE` when the root may match the empty
// string or the set holds more than `NREGEX_LITERAL_LIMIT` bytes; and the inner literal when it has a byte.
func:extract_literals = NIL(Hir->:h) never fails {
    uint32:root = raw hir_props(h, h.root);
    bool:whole = raw prefix_bytes(h);
    int64:plen = h.lits.count;
    if (plen > 0i64) {
        int64:role = HIR_LITERAL_PREFIX;
        if (whole) { role = HIR_LITERAL_WHOLE; }
        drop vec_push(@h.literals, Literal{ role: role, off: 0i64, len: plen });
    }
    if ((root & HIR_CAN_MATCH_EMPTY) != 0u32) {
        drop vec_push(@h.literals, Literal{ role: HIR_LITERAL_ANYWHERE, off: plen, len: 0i64 });
    }
    else {
        ByteSet:s = raw byteset_empty();
        drop first_bytes(h, @s);
        int64:c = raw byteset_count(@s);
        if (c > NREGEX_LITERAL_LIMIT) {
            drop vec_push(@h.literals, Literal{ role: HIR_LITERAL_ANYWHERE, off: plen, len: 0i64 });
        }
        else {
            int64:off = h.lits.count;
            int64:b = raw byteset_next(@s, 0i64);
            while (b < 256i64) decreases 256i64 - b {
                drop vec_push(@h.lits, b =>! uint8);
                b = raw byteset_next(@s, b + 1i64);
            }
            drop vec_push(@h.literals, Literal{ role: HIR_LITERAL_FIRST, off: off, len: c });
        }
    }
    drop inner_literal(h, 0i64, plen);
    pass NIL;
};

// obligation: never fails requires h.root != HIR_NONE
//
// THE QUERY (H-20): the Hir's literals, extracted first -- once -- when it holds none, and how many it holds.
// An extraction always writes the first-byte set's entry, so a Hir that holds none has not had its literals
// extracted: the distinct "not yet extracted" state, never "no literal" (the compiler's D-227). A `Hir` with no
// root has no tree to extract from, and the extraction's first step, the root's facts, stops it `OutOfBounds`.
pub func:hir_literals = int64(Hir->:h) never fails {
    if (h.literals.count == 0i64) { drop extract_literals(h); }
    pass h.literals.count;
};

// obligation: never fails ensures result == h.literals.count
//
// How many literals the Hir holds, extracting none: 0 until `hir_literals` has run -- "not yet", never "none".
pub func:hir_literal_count = int64(Hir:h) never fails {
    pass h.literals.count;
};

// obligation: never fails requires k >= 0i64 && k < hir_literal_count(h)
pub func:hir_literal = Literal(Hir:h, int64:k) never fails {
    pass raw vec_get(h.literals, k);
};

// obligation: never fails requires at >= 0i64 && at < h.lits.count
//
// A byte of the Hir's literals: an entry's are `hir_literal_byte(h, l.off + i)`, `0 <= i < l.len`.
pub func:hir_literal_byte = uint8(Hir:h, int64:at) never fails {
    pass raw vec_get(h.lits, at);
};

// obligation: never fails ensures h.root == HIR_NONE
//
// Frees the arena's blocks. A node, a range and a group own nothing, so each block is its
// whole obligation, and a unit that frees and exits 0 proves it (D-151: a leaked `wild`
// block traps at exit); `names` is managed and drops with the `Hir`.
// *(2026-10-15, cycle 0.2.5 -- RX-242: and the literals' two blocks, `literals` and `lits`: a `Literal` and a byte
// own nothing too.)*
pub func:hir_free = NIL(Hir->:h) never fails {
    drop vec_free(@h.nodes);
    drop vec_free(@h.ranges);
    drop vec_free(@h.groups);
    drop vec_free(@h.literals);
    drop vec_free(@h.lits);
    h.root = HIR_NONE;
    pass NIL;
};
